<section class="lede">
  <h1>The Cayo Smooth Expedition</h1>
  <p class="lede__text">
    In 1979 an A&amp;R man named Gil Vandermeer chartered a fifty-two-foot
    ketch, loaded it with a Fender Rhodes, four studio musicians, an
    unlicensed dentist, and roughly nine hundred pounds of provisions that
    were legally classified as &ldquo;cheese,&rdquo; and set sail for what he
    described in a telegram as &ldquo;the smooth latitudes.&rdquo;
  </p>
  <p class="lede__text">
    They were gone for fourteen months. They came back with sixty-one songs
    and no ketch. This Archive holds the recovered materials.
  </p>
  <p class="more"><a href="{{ '/expedition/field-report/' | url }}">Read the field report</a></p>
</section>

